      "input": {
        "source": "kk:review-findings",
        "content": "Pattern: \"Simplification\" that deletes an ownership/epoch guard before a destructive operation introduces a correctness regression. Example: cleanup_setup(store, workspace_id, setup_id) originally guarded `store.active.pop(workspace_id)` with `if association and association[\"setup_id\"] == setup_id`. The guard ensures a stale cleanup for an OLD setup does not delete the active association now owned by a NEWER setup for the same workspace. Removing the guard makes the pop unconditional, so a late cleanup of a superseded setup tears down a live, valid connection. Red flag: diff deletes a conditional whose predicate compares an identity/epoch field (setup_id/version/generation) before pop/delete/write. Also watch for tests whose NAME claims the guarded semantics (\"removes its OWN association\") but only exercise the matching case, giving false green coverage. Fix: keep the ownership check, or only remove the association if it still belongs to the setup being cleaned up."
      },
